@startuml ebpf_architecture
title eBPF — load-time preparation and event-time execution
rectangle "User space loader\n(libbpf / bpf syscall)" as loader
rectangle "Kernel verifier" as verifier
rectangle "JIT native code\n(if supported/enabled)" as jit
rectangle "Interpreter\n(where supported)" as interp
rectangle "Attached hook\n(event occurs)" as hook
rectangle "Program execution\n(abstract BPF runtime)" as run
database "BPF maps" as maps
loader --> verifier : load bytecode; validate
verifier --> jit : prepare one execution path
verifier --> interp : alternative execution path
loader --> hook : attach verified program
hook --> run : invoke on event
jit ..> run : native implementation
interp ..> run : interpreted implementation
run --> maps : lookup/update through permitted helpers
loader --> maps : permitted user-space map operations
legend bottom
Solid labelled edges: preparation, attachment or invocation as stated.
Dotted edges: alternative implementations of the abstract runtime.
JIT-native execution does not then require an interpreter stage.
endlegend
@enduml
